# zdev projects — one path per line, relative to $ZDEV_WORKSPACE (default
# ~/workspace). Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# TWO MODES:
#
# Classic (default): this file is the whole registry — every project is a
# line here.
#
# Discovery (ZDEV_PROJECTS_DISCOVER=1 in ~/.config/zdev/env): the workspace
# layout is the registry and this file holds OVERRIDES only —
#
#   Two questions decide everything, and neither is answered in config:
#   1. root dir WITH .git      → a plain project row (zdev, dotfiles)
#      root dir WITHOUT .git   → a GROUP
#   2. group WITH INITIATIVE.md → an INITIATIVE: its own dir rows as the
#                                 group home, plus one row per child that
#                                 has .git (so notes/ never rows)
#      group WITHOUT it         → a DRAWER: one row per child dir, any dir
#                                 (e.g. projects/)
#   `touch <group>/INITIATIVE.md` promotes a drawer; deleting it demotes.
#
# The daemon watches the workspace: `git clone` into a group IS add-repo,
# `rm -rf` is remove — rows follow the disk in seconds.
# `zdev --list-projects -v` shows why every row exists.
#
# Either mode: append ' *' to mark a favorite — started by `zdev up`,
# never reaped:
#   projects/backend *
#
# Replace the examples below with your own (delete them entirely under
# discovery unless you want favorites or off-convention paths).
dotfiles
projects/api
projects/web *
